    "extraction_notes": [
      "This is a p-channel enhancement MOSFET. All curve and numeric voltage/current values are represented as positive magnitudes; original negative signs are retained in conditions and specs.polarity = p.",
      "The electrical table publishes RDS(ON) typical and maximum values. The strict schema records the MAX values: 85 mOhm at VGS = -10 V, ID = -3 A, and 120 mOhm at VGS = -4.5 V, ID = -2 A. Typical values are 73 mOhm and 98 mOhm respectively.",
      "Transfer curve is at VDS = -5 V and includes Ta = 25 degC and 125 degC traces; the 25 degC trace was digitized. Output curves are at Ta = 25 degC for VGS = -3, -3.5, -4, -4.5, -5, -6, -7, and -10 V; representative -4.5, -6, and -10 V curves are digitized.",
      "Capacitance table values are typical at VDS = -20 V, VGS = 0 V, f = 1 MHz: Ciss = 600 pF, Coss = 90 pF, Crss = 70 pF. Figure 10 was digitized separately for the voltage dependence.",
      "Gate-charge table values: Qg = 14 nC, Qgs = 2.9 nC, Qgd = 3.8 nC typical at VDS = -20 V, ID = -3 A, VGS = -10 V. Switching times are typical: td(on) = 9 ns, tr = 8 ns, td(off) = 28 ns, tf = 10 ns under the stated test circuit conditions.",
      "Body-diode forward voltage is VSD = 1.2 V maximum at VGS = 0 V and IS = -3.3 A. No body-diode reverse-recovery time or reverse-recovery charge is published.",
      "Absolute maximum ratings: VDS = -40 V, VGS = +/-20 V, ID = -5 A continuous, ID = -2.3 A at TC = 100 degC, IDM = -18 A pulsed, PD = 1.4 W, TJ/TSTG = -55 to +150 degC, and RthetaJA = 89 degC/W on FR4."
    ],
